{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cache as database cache as database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md","fileName":"Cache as Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cache as Database","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 11:51\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cache as database cache as database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md","fileName":"Cache as Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cache as Database","heading":"Cache as Database","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Using a cache as a database makes a low-latency cache technology the authoritative store for a bounded set of application data. Redis can support such a design when its persistence, replication, and recovery guarantees match the consequence of losing state.\n\nThe decision differs from ordinary caching because there may be no slower source from which to reconstruct a missing value. Eviction and expiration must therefore be disabled or designed as intentional data lifecycle behavior.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cache as Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceS